Maybe not a lot.<p>Showboat documents look neater if there are single one-line commands that do something useful. Dumping a full Playwright script into a cell is less readable.<p>Showboat also has a special feature where you can embed an image directly in the document by running:<p><pre><code>  showboat image doc.md &#x27;rodney screenshot&#x27;
</code></pre>
The command you call should return a path to an image file as the last line of output. Rodney does exactly that.<p>It may well turn out that Rodney is unnecessary and people find better patterns using Showboat with existing tools like playwright-cli - in which case it won&#x27;t matter because Showboat and Rodney aren&#x27;t coupled to each other at all.<p>Showboat is definitely the more significant of the two projects.
